WEBVTT

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.460
Let's go, everyone!

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.540
Yeah!

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.010
<i>Why...</i>

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.300
<i>Why did you come here?</i>

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.020
<b>Flag 13</b>

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.020
<b>If His Flag Breaks</b>

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:50.080
I-It's not like I'm going 
to sing for Hatate.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.930
Someone once told me that

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.770
my songs can give hope to everyone.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.700
That's the only reason!

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.880
I'm not able to do anything,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.510
but I'll dance and cheer you all on! I will!

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.550
Watch me, Souta-oniisama!

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.700
I swear on our manly friendship

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.520
that I shall take care 
of Souta-kun's enemies!

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.710
Souta-san said he needed me!

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.950
I need him, too,

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.740
if that's okay with him!

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.700
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.520
<i>You were out here by yourself,</i>

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.170
<i>and I wasn't able to be 
a big sister for you.</i>

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.570
<i>But...</i>

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.390
<i>It'll be okay now.</i>

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.260
<i>Your big sister will protect you!</i>

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.040
Any one who makes Souta boy cry...

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.100
will be getting a spanking from me!

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.480
Older sisters aren't the only ones

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.230
who get to save onii-chan!

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.120
I am not part of the Council of 
the Seven Virtues any longer!

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.280
I'm Hatate Souta's Samurai.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.260
Daimyouzamurai Mei!

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.580
Were you the ones giving 
Souta a hard time?!

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.640
Even if I'm from a parallel world,

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.830
I'm me!

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.460
Hatate-kun, I'm going 
to save you this time!

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.660
Bullying Souta is against school rules!

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.260
Student Council President Punch!

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.690
Why did you come...

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.680
I can't repay you for this...

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.440
That's not true!

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.400
I... got something

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.070
very special from you.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:09.500
I was empty when I couldn't 
see that girl anymore,

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.540
for a long time.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.640
But I met you,

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.760
and I wanted to save you.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.500
I wanted to hear your voice.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.510
I wanted to see your smile.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.550
You had me experience all 
of those wonderful feelings,

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.430
and that made me

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.770
who I am today.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.280
I love you, Souta-kun.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.950
I'm sure Nanami-chan and 
the rest feel the same.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.290
Take that!

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.480
I can't match them.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:00.800
It can't be.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.300
They're nothing more 
than virtual people.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:14.950
What's going on?

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.000
It's absorbing its 
allies and powering up.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.570
This is the last boss flag!

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.520
This is the Angel Boat...

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.780
Rin-kun! Granny! Prez!

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.880
Okiku-nee! Megumu! Ruri!

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.440
<i>This isn't going to work.</i>

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.030
<i>I'm not going to make it there.</i>

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.040
<i>The main server's going to be...</i>

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.610
<i>Everyone's going to be...</i>

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.930
<i>Can I do something...</i>

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.190
<i>Is there some sort of special</i>

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.010
<i>death flag I can use to defeat that?</i>

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.310
<i>Oh, there is.</i>

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.880
<i>There's a special death 
flag I can use right here!</i>

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.410
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.300
<i>Something's coming inside me.</i>

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:15.900
<i>This is...</i>

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.050
<i>This is...</i>

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.130
<i>This is the truth</i>

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.220
<i>behind the Premium 
Ambriel that I had forgotten.</i>

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.550
<i>Where everything began...</i>

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.260
Are we going to die here?!

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.150
I don't want to die...

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.480
I just got to be friends 
with all of you and Souta-kun...

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.220
Get a hold of yourself, Okiku!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.050
It'll be fine!

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.390
I'm sure we'll all be okay!

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.590
My brother is right!

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.140
We shouldn't give up yet!

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.690
If we reach the deck, I'm sure 
there'll be lifeboats available.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.590
If we can just make it to one of those...

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.790
What's wrong, Sou-kun?

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.670
You shouldn't start spacing out right now.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.020
Are you alone?

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:16.150
Where are your parents?

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.540
Souta-kun, is something over there?

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:20.770
Huh?

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.490
It's dangerous to go alone!

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:27.250
Watch out!

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:28.610
This way!

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:40.930
We're...

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.560
I hope everything's okay.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.190
Why are you trying to save me?

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.330
Why?

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.690
It's only natural to try and save someone.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.110
Save someone...

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.490
So what's your name?

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.580
Me?

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.600
I'm Laplace's Demon.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.120
Nice to meet you,

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.630
Hatate Souta-san.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.250
Why do you know my name?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.050
Is someone there?!

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.180
Save me!

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.010
Are you okay?!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.680
I'll lift that off of you.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:18.930
Th-Thanks.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.180
I can't move.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.440
H-Hurry.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:27.960
R-Right.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:29.940
Thanks.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:31.180
You saved me.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.360
N-No...

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.860
Anyway, we need to get out of here now.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.360
H-Hey!

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:08.650
Are you okay?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.150
Yeah, I think so...

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:22.010
I-I can't do anything...

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.310
I'm going to get some help.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.010
Wait just a second!

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:27.170
N-No!

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.610
I'll be right back! I will!

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.670
W-Wait!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:31.970
Wait!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.830
Wait!

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:00.780
Only natural to try and save someone?

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.380
That's right.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:06.560
It is.

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:11.110
He's going to get some help.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.040
He told me to wait here.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.420
So... So, I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.430
It will.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:27.310
It seems this is the end for you.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.270
It doesn't seem like anyone will come.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.310
No...

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:35.490
But why...

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:39.320
Betrayed by the person you saved.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.070
How does it feel?

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.490
No, I don't want to die.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.220
I don't want to

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:48.310
die here alone...

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.970
I guess humans are the same, 
no matter the world.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.870
It doesn't seem like there's anything 
left to see in this world.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.300
Souta!

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:05.560
Sou-kun!

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.510
Sorry I'm late!

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.850
It's okay. We'll get you out now.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.310
All right, we're going to lift this thing.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.320
We're going to save you, Sou-kun!

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:17.820
Let's go.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.060
One... Two...

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.650
One.. two...

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:27.830
<i>Why did I...</i>

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:31.900
<i>Why did I doubt them...</i>

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.590
One... Two...

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.140
Everyone, watch out!

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.560
<i>Is everyone going to die here...</i>

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:50.610
<i>Is that</i>

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:52.750
<i>their fate?!</i>

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:57.700
What if I told you there was a

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.010
way to change their fate?

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:00.810
Huh?

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.360
At this rate everyone will die.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.370
This is proof of that.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.630
This is?

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:09.690
This is a death flag.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:11.070
A death flag?

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:14.660
A flag is a mechanism that 
causes a branch in fate.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:18.590
No one can escape its influence.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.600
Except for one of you.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.250
Hatate Souta,

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:24.800
you have no death flag.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.210
You're also the only one

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:32.180
who can alter everyone's fate.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.940
What do I...

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:36.980
It's simple.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.160
Collect everyone's death flags into one,

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.330
and carry their fate for them.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.980
In other words, this.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.840
Everyone's life is not equal.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:06.220
You shall be tormented 
by every sort of despair,

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.730
and reach closer and closer to death.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.350
That's the price to save everyone.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.920
Will everyone be saved?

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:28.530
Yes, I promise you.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:33.640
Give everyone's

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.750
death flags to me.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:38.770
Very well.

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:40.250
And one more thing.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:44.510
I will erase this event 
from everyone's memories.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:47.590
You will never have met them.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.920
You will live in solitude,

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.260
and hate yourself for the choice you made,

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.010
hate the people who put you through a living hell,

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:59.520
or perhaps hate the world itself for making you experience this,

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.130
and while cursing them all, 
live out your final days.

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:07.230
<i>I won't curse them.</i>

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.280
<i>I already know...</i>

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:14.120
<i>I know the hearts of everyone 
in this world are so beautiful.</i>

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:17.340
<i>That's why no matter how 
much I give in to despair.</i>

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.590
<i>I will continue to exclaim,</i>

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.880
<i>just how beautiful the world is!</i>

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:30.700
To you, fear and despair.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.690
And to them, a loss of memory and life.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.680
I won't leave Souta-kun alone!

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.230
I'll find you, no matter where you are!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.520
I will find you! I will!

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.570
I'll start looking for you right away!

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:48.200
I'll be waiting for you, Souta!

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:50.830
<i>That will never happen.</i>

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:53.530
<i>But thank you.</i>

00:14:57.570 --> 00:15:00.460
<i>My death flag collected the fate of death
from many others.</i>

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:01.740
<i>I see...</i>

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.710
<i>So all of that was for this?</i>

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.970
<i>I still can't make it!</i>

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.480
<i>Is my life not enough to reach them?!</i>

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:16.230
<i>Can I not protect them all?</i>

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.220
<i>I see.</i>

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:36.470
<i>So everyone kept their promise.</i>

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.700
Where am I...

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:21.480
So you've awoken, Hatate Souta.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.000
You're...

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:26.170
This is the real world.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:27.580
The real world?

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:29.740
Then the battle...

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:30.950
What about everyone?

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:34.070
There is still some chaos remaining from the

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.750
rampage of the Angel Boat 
and its destruction,

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:38.800
but it's mostly peaceful.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:40.930
You won.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:43.740
I see.

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:48.240
Before entered Hatagaya Academy, 
you were involved in an accident,

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.460
and traveled the boundaries 
between life and death.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.980
I used your consciousness to connect

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:55.070
to many different virtual worlds,

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:58.830
and used you to help fight 
against the Angel Boat.

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:02.960
And then you met the Sacrament 
and Laplace's Demon.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.850
You know about them?!

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:09.520
Those are emotion programs that the

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.960
Angel Boat cut off when it started 
its rebellion against humanity.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:13.650
Programs...

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.220
You could call them its conscience.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:20.220
The Council of the Seven Virtues 
ran several simulations,

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:23.220
and in those virtual worlds, 
we also simulated them, as well.

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:24.730
Why?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:28.230
To find a way for humanity 
to resist the Angel Boat.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:30.730
To save us...

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:35.200
Laplace's Demon's affinity towards those with 
strong hearts and a strong sense of sacrifice,

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.490
and the Sacrament's affinity towards the bonds

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.460
that are created between 
people were something

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.980
we thought we needed to reach the Angel Boat.

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:45.620
And you know the rest.

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:49.580
Bonds, huh?

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:54.010
Humanity may have been tested.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:59.360
Would we become the slaves 
of a mechanical system that ruled the network?

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.510
Or would we join hands,

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.500
and live?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.600
N-Nanami?!

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.160
Thinking on it,

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:12.440
I've only lived to protect my homeland.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.530
I'm not any different from the Angel Boat.

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:16.710
I've lived a long time.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:19.030
I didn't think I'd be saved 
by what I cast aside.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.830
I, Number Zero— No,

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.820
Kagura Bladefield wish to extend my deepest gratitude, Hatate Souta.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.090
So you're the founder of Bladefield?!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.130
One last thing...

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.760
The days you spent in the virtual world

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.970
were incredibly short in reality.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.100
No one shares those 
memories of yours, either.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.550
Princess Nanami, who dived into to the

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.850
virtual world to save you, is no exception.

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:51.450
I have no intention of asking 
you to forgive me, but...

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:55.260
Farewell, Prince.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.990
Souta!

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:15.880
Nanami?!

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:23.350
I'm your older sister and you 
didn't call me "oneesan"? Why?!

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.640
I'm sorry,

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:27.640
Neesan.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:33.780
<i>We're not sure what caused the</i>

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:36.960
<i>global network disruptions the other day.</i>

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.570
<i>However, we're starting to see all</i>

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.770
<i>vital infrastructure returning to normal.</i>

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:10.560
Huh?

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.320
A-Akane?

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:17.230
Um, have we met before?

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.860
No, sorry. My mistake.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.870
I'm not anyone weird.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.870
I'll be moving into this dorm.

00:20:25.130 --> 00:20:26.200
Really?!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.690
Me, too!

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:31.440
I'm Mahougasawa Akane.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.500
Nice to meet you.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.210
Yeah, nice to meet you.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.890
My name's Hatate Souta.

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.170
Well, let's go exploring Quest Dorm!

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:42.720
Yeah.

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:46.810
I wonder which room I should pick.

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.020
They're all the same inside.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:51.240
How do you know?

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:54.400
Well, I think the corner 
room might be taken already.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.000
Really?

00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:59.600
I guess I'll go take a look 
at the room over there, then!

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:07.500
Akane!

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:21.380
Um, Hatate-kun?

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:24.690
Thank goodness...

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.080
Huh?

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.270
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:38.650
You saved me again, Souta-kun.

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.050
You were able

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:46.270
to keep your promise again.

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:50.380
Yes.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.290
Humans are strange.

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:59.030
Humans easily exceed our expectations.

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:01.220
I'm sure that's why they're so precious.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:04.300
Yes, they taught us that.

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:05.300
This world is

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:08.560
so beautiful.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:12.600
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:36.370
I'm thinking of proposing to her once

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:38.930
this business deal goes through.

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:41.130
Well, that's a reason to celebrate.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Thanks for your support!</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
Illustration: CUTEG
